# NFL photo jersey backs (always)

**One silhouette.** Bulky NFL yoke cut with shoulder nameplate, short sleeves with stripe bands, side helmet in frame. Solid `#000` (LED energy). No hanger on photo backs.

**Wordmark:** baked into the PNG only (club name on the yoke plate, never the patron name or number). Upright block caps heat-transfer on the yoke — not italic, not arched like soccer. Letter color = kit secondary. CSS must **not** reprint the team name on photo kits (`.soccer-jersey-team` hidden when `usePhotoBack`).

**Collar:** PNG must show the full collar/neckline band above the yoke. Do not crop the top of the jersey in the asset. QA: collar visible on `led-64x32` before Pages.

**Helmet:** gold (or kit secondary) helmet on the **right** side, partially overlapping the jersey hem. Helmet bottom must sit **well above** the image bottom edge (~8%+ margin) so `display.css` scaling does not clip the facemask.

**Patron name overlay:** CSS only (`#displayMain.soccer-jersey-name`). Upright Impact / condensed caps. Sit **halfway** between the PNG yoke wordmark bottom and the number box top. Photo-back CSS: name `top` ~18% (96×48 / 64×48 ~17%, 64×32 ~16%); `height` ~9%; `font-size` cap ~11.5vh (one notch above soccer photo kits).

**Number overlay:** CSS only (`#displaySub.soccer-jersey-number`). Huge upright condensed mark, horizontally center-justified. `top` ~40% (96×48 ~39%, 64×32 ~38%); `height` ~28%; `align-content: center` (not end — prevents 50vh glyphs from climbing into the name). Cap ~48vh. Same horizontal inset as the name.

**Background layer:** `background-size: 82% auto`; `background-position: center 36%` — shows collar at top and keeps helmet in frame.

## FIX PROMPT — CSS hanger vs named photo

Same as soccer: a named PNG **always** wins. Catalog `defaultBackgroundUrl` = `images/nfl/nfl-{slug}-back-with-club.png`, `jerseyCssBack: false`. Ship PNGs on **`origin/main`**.

